  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the most favorable outcomes among those with the highest probability in each lottery. However, the individual considers all outcomes and probabilities to compute expected values, and bases the decision on which lottery has the higher expected payout. This is a different decision rule (expected value maximization) than the one specified in the decision reason (most probable outcome comparison). The information considered overlaps partially (outcomes and probabilities), but the rule used by the individual is clearly different. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
